# Agent Memory Subsystem 🧠

This directory handles the state, context, and persistence of the proactive agent. It is divided into three distinct modules to separate the ephemeral conversation buffer from long-term vector storage, managed by a central orchestration layer.

## Architecture Overview

```text
memory/
├── README.md
├── short_memory.py   # Ephemeral conversation state (Sliding windows)
├── long_memory.py    # Persistent semantic memory (Pinecone)
└── memory_logic.py   # Orchestration and extraction logic (The API)


1. short_memory.py (The Working Buffer)
Purpose: Manages the immediate conversational context and the active session state. This is fast, volatile memory that gets wiped or summarized when it gets too long.

Key Responsibilities:

Storing the last N messages of the conversation.

Enforcing token limits (sliding window or truncation).

Tracking the current active plan or step the user is on.

Expected Functions/Classes:

class SessionBuffer:

add_message(session_id, role, content) -> Appends to the buffer.

get_recent_history(session_id, k=10) -> Retrieves the window for the LLM.

clear_session(session_id) -> Wipes the buffer.

Dependencies: typing, standard in-memory structures (dict), or redis if scaling.

2. long_memory.py (The Vector Vault)
Purpose: Handles all communication with the vector database. It strictly deals with embeddings, semantic search, and persistent storage.

Key Responsibilities:

Initializing the Pinecone client and connecting to the index.

Generating embeddings from text.

Upserting facts into the correct user namespaces.

Querying for semantically relevant past notes.

Expected Functions/Classes:

class VectorStore:

_get_embedding(text) -> Calls the embedding API.

save_note(user_id, topic, content) -> Upserts to Pinecone.

retrieve_context(user_id, current_query, top_k) -> Returns matching notes.

Dependencies: pinecone, embedding library (e.g., openai, langchain-huggingface).

3. memory_logic.py (The Orchestrator)
Purpose: This is the "Brain" of the memory system. It acts as the bridge between short_memory.py, long_memory.py, and the main FastAPI routing endpoints. The rest of the backend should only import from this file.

Key Responsibilities:

Context Assembly: Combining retrieved notes from long_memory with the recent history from short_memory into a single prompt block.

The Triage Pipeline: Running the background logic (or small LLM call) to decide if a new user message contains a permanent fact worth extracting to long_memory.

API Interface: Providing clean, high-level methods for main.py.

Expected Functions/Classes:

class MemoryManager: (Imports SessionBuffer and VectorStore)

process_user_input(session_id, user_id, message) -> Triggers triage and updates short-term.

build_agent_prompt(session_id, user_id, current_query) -> Assembles the context payload for the main ReAct loop.

handle_explicit_feedback(user_id, feedback_data) -> Bypasses triage and forces a save to Pinecone.

Dependencies: short_memory, long_memory, LLM client for extraction logic.